Hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:

>[] Unless we assume that all females in general, and all nymphs in
>[] particular, are lesbian, isn't it a bit silly to have the "bea-
>[] tiful" nymphs able to steal from female characters with the same
>[] ease as the males.
>
>Clearly the current situation could be handled "better", however the
>attack of a nymph versus a male is seduction (sexual) and versus
>a female is charm (charismatic).  That these are equally effective
>is open to debate but the current situation seems balanced and doesn't
>resort to assuming lesbianism, etc.

Yes, I can see that explanation as possible, but it strikes me as more
of an excuse than a rationale for reasons why the code was written as
it was.

>It would be neater (in my opinion) if the attack of the nymph class
>(let's say female nymphs and male satyrs) was strictly sexual.  i'd
>like it more if being "ugly" or "too attractive" caused problems.
>however, that is probably more controversial ...

I agree.  It would add a nice touch if one's sex came more into play
during the game.  Women are lighter and weaker than men - on the aver-
age.  Yet they tend to be hardier under long-term duress, and are ca-
pable of greater stealth.  They also have lower caloric requirements,
and it can be argued that their lower testosterone levels make them
inherently less likely to be incited to violence.

I "vote" that women be immune to numphs, take much longer to get hungry
than men, that they be more resistent to certain poisons, that they
have slightly greater overall charisma, and that they be capable of
greater stealth.  There is room for a lot of possibilities regarding
their interactions with non-lycanthropic and non-chaotic males of es-
pecially the human variety.  Most males won't walk up and whomp a
female.  I think the women should always be able to get the first blow
in on a (human) male.  After all, men typically underestimate women.
And, so many of them tell us, we are led around by our dicks anyway.
It would, at any rate, make up for some of the size disadvantage....

The men, in turn, would be somewhat stronger, with a slightly greater
constitution (short-term ability to withstand injury).  They would
need much more food, though (about a third more), and could be seduced
by nymphs and such.  Although this is debatable, one might argue that
their charisma should be slightly lower, and that they would not so
easily attain stealth, but they would be faster at least.

Obviously not all of these things could be easily quantified.  It is
also possible to get overly subtle with such matters.  There are so
many subtle interactions already in NetHack that it is hard to sort them
all out as it is.  Sex, though, is a very important characteristic, and
it needs to be taken account, I think.

-Richard


